<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00493">
	<title>Lane Keeping Assist malfunction</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e03341">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e03342">
								<image href="images/OCL4M055096N.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03343">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Check Driver Assistance system</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>When Lane Keeping Assist is not working properly, the Master warning light (<image href="images/WKIA_040.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>), and the yellow indicator (<image href="images/WKIA_198.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>) light appear on the instrument cluster, along with a warning message.</p>
		<p>If a warning message appears, have the Lane Keeping Assist function inspected by a professional workshop. Kia recommends visiting an authorized Kia dealer or service partner.</p>
	</conbody>
